- Relationship between father and newborn: Good or Very good relationship likely reduces risk; Bad or Neutral relationship may increase risk.  
- Education Level: Higher education (University, College) may provide better coping skills, reducing risk; lower education may increase risk.  
- Number of household members: Larger household (6 to 8, 9 or more) may imply more social support, reducing risk; smaller household (2 to 5) may increase risk.

